<body>
<div class="layout">
<header class="topbar"><a class="brand" href="#" aria-label="Sahasra Guardian"><span class="brand-symbol">G</span><span class="brand-label">guardian<span>by Sahasra</span></span></a>
<nav class="nav hidden" id="nav"><button class="active" data-view="overview">Overview</button><button data-view="diagnostics">Diagnostics</button><button data-view="playbooks">Playbooks</button><button data-view="heal">Heal</button><button data-view="ops">Ops</button><button data-view="help">Help / How to use</button></nav>
<div class="topright"><span class="top-status"><i class="dot" id="onlineDot"></i><span id="onlineText">Locked</span></span><button class="linkbtn hidden" id="acctButton">Account</button><button class="linkbtn hidden" id="logoutButton">Sign out</button></div></header>
<main>
<section id="loginView" class="login-wrap section"><div class="login-shell"><div class="login-story"><div><div class="kicker">AthenTech support operations</div><h1>Keep every LIS client running. Without the complexity.</h1><p>Quiet monitoring, clear diagnostics, and practical recovery steps for your Sahasra AI Agent.</p></div><div class="login-caption">A focused workspace. No changes to client data.</div></div>
<div class="login-form"><div class="kicker">Restricted access</div><h2>Welcome back.</h2><p class="intro">Sign in with your existing Sahasra admin account.</p><form id="loginFormG" autocomplete="on" onsubmit="return false"><label class="field" for="username">Username</label><input class="input" id="username" name="username" autocomplete="username" placeholder="Enter your username"><label class="field" for="password">Password</label><input class="input" id="password" name="password" type="password" autocomplete="current-password" placeholder="Enter your password"><button type="submit" class="btn primary full" style="margin-top:25px;padding:14px" id="loginButton">Continue to Guardian <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></form><div class="notice" role="status" id="loginNotice"></div><p style="font-size:11px;color:#a1aaa3;margin:19px 0 0">Having trouble signing in? The Help page is available after successful authentication.</p></div></div></section>
<div id="workspace" class="hidden">
<section class="section" id="overviewView"><div class="page-head"><div><div class="kicker">Your command overview</div><h1>A clearer picture of your system.</h1><p>Everything that needs attention, and nothing that doesn't. Client issues are isolated; troubleshooting actions are deliberately safe.</p></div><div class="actions"><button class="btn" id="downloadButton">Download support report</button><button class="btn primary" id="refreshButton">Refresh status ↻</button></div></div>
<section class="fix-center" id="fixCenter"><div class="fix-header"><div><div class="doc-label">Interactive troubleshooting</div><h2 class="fix-title">What isn't working?</h2><p class="fix-sub">Paste an error message or pick a common issue. Guardian gives you safe, simple steps—no AI subscription needed.</p></div><span class="pill">Guided · read-only</span></div><div class="fix-inputs"><input id="fixIssue" type="text" maxlength="600" aria-label="Describe the problem" placeholder="Example: Login says Unexpected token < or collections show zero"><button class="btn primary" id="fixFind" type="button">Find a solution →</button></div><div class="fix-picks"><button type="button" data-symptom="SQL Server won't connect">Database connection</button><button type="button" data-symptom="Unexpected token HTML JSON">Login / IIS</button><button type="button" data-symptom="wrong collection amounts">Wrong totals</button><button type="button" data-symptom="TAT compliance unavailable">TAT / SLA</button><button type="button" data-symptom="LLM route intent wrong">Intent / AI</button><button type="button" data-symptom="PDF export failed">PDF / Excel</button><button type="button" data-symptom="schema invalid column">Schema changed</button><button type="button" data-symptom="502 service unavailable">Service offline</button></div><div id="fixAnswer" class="fix-answer hidden" aria-live="polite"></div></section><div class="kpis"><div class="kpi"><div class="kpi-label">Clients with recorded issues</div><div class="kpi-value" id="errorCount">—</div><div class="kpi-foot">Based on available Guardian events</div></div><div class="kpi"><div class="kpi-label">Temporarily paused clients</div><div class="kpi-value" id="pausedCount">—</div><div class="kpi-foot">Circuit breaker protection</div></div><div class="kpi"><div class="kpi-label">Guardian API</div><div class="kpi-value smallvalue" id="systemStatus">Connecting…</div><div class="kpi-foot">Current authenticated connection</div></div></div>
<div class="two-col"><article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><h2>Recent signals</h2><p>Client-specific incidents with next actions</p></div><span class="pill">Read-only</span></div><div class="panel-content" id="statusArea"><div class="empty">Loading incidents…</div></div></article><article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><h2>Where to start</h2><p>Simple steps when something isn't working</p></div></div><div class="panel-content"><div class="guidance"><div class="step"><span class="num">01</span><div><b>Find the affected client</b><p>Check recent signals or enter its activation code in Diagnostics.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span class="num">02</span><div><b>Run a safe self-check</b><p>Guardian examines connection and supported schema details.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span class="num">03</span><div><b>Follow the suggested recovery</b><p>Use Playbooks for practical, non-destructive steps.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span class="num">04</span><div><b>Escalate if still failing</b><p>Download a sanitized support report for a developer.</p></div></div></div><button class="btn soft full" style="margin-top:24px" data-go="help">Open the complete guide →</button></div></article></div></section>
<section class="section hidden" id="diagnosticsView"><div class="page-head"><div><div class="kicker">Client investigation</div><h1>Diagnostics, without guesswork.</h1><p>Choose a client and perform one focused check at a time. Checks read data; they do not edit LIS tables.</p></div></div><article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><h2>Select a client</h2><p>Use the activation code associated with the institution.</p></div></div><div class="panel-content"><div class="client-form"><div><label class="field" for="clientCode" style="margin-top:0">Client activation code</label><input class="input" id="clientCode" type="password" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Enter activation code"></div><button class="btn primary" id="selfcheck">Run self-check →</button></div><div class="button-row"><button class="btn" id="diagnostics">View schema diagnostics</button><button class="btn" id="snapshot">Compare schema snapshot</button><button class="btn soft" id="refreshSchema">Refresh cached profile</button></div><div class="control-explain">
<details><summary>What is schema diagnostics?</summary><p>Shows which tables and columns Guardian has detected, the effective collection metric, available report capabilities, and rejected client configuration pins. Use it when a report is wrong or unavailable.</p></details>
<details><summary>What is schema snapshot comparison?</summary><p>Compares today's detected database columns with the previous recorded snapshot to highlight newly added or missing fields. It may update Guardian's local snapshot metadata, but not the client's LIS tables.</p></details>
<details><summary>Why refresh cached profile?</summary><p>Sahasra keeps detected mappings in memory for up to six hours. Refresh only the selected client's profile after a verified schema/config change. It does not rewrite client records.</p></details>
</div><div class="fix-alert">Not sure what a failed check means? Each failed check now suggests a guided fix. You can also use the Fix Center on Overview.</div><div class="notice" id="actionNotice" role="status"></div><div class="report hidden" id="clientResultWrap"><div class="report-head" id="resultTitle">Diagnostic results</div><div id="clientResult"></div></div></div></article><div class="hint-box" style="margin-top:18px"><h3>What happens when you refresh a profile?</h3><p>Only the selected client's cached schema mapping is refreshed. The underlying client SQL Server tables are not changed. If a check reports a missing field, open Playbooks before making any configuration changes.</p></div></section>
<section class="section hidden" id="playbooksView"><div class="page-head"><div><div class="kicker">Practical recovery</div><h1>One problem. Clear steps.</h1><p>Choose the issue you are facing. Each guide stays collapsed until you need it.</p></div></div><div class="searchbar"><svg width="19" height="19" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m20 20-4-4"/></svg><input id="playbookSearch" type="search" aria-label="Search help and recovery playbooks" placeholder="Search: database offline, 404, Excel, payment, PDF, login…"><span class="search-hint">Smart help search</span></div><p class="search-help">Browse 130 guides. Search by symptom or error message. This local guided search is not an AI diagnosis. Results are ranked by matching topics and keywords; no client data leaves this page.</p><div class="result-count" id="playbookCount"></div><div class="playbooks-list" id="playbooksList"><details class="playbook" id="pb-llm-latency" data-keywords="llm ai latency slow response time delayed provider token generation"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>LLM responses are slow / high latency</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Compare a known direct report with an open-ended AI question. If only AI is slow, the database probably is not the bottleneck.</li><li>Record response duration and approximate prompt/output length without saving patient data.</li><li>Check provider status, timeouts, token limits and concurrent request load with your administrator.</li><li>Escalate slow model response or provider/network delays; do not change client LIS data.</li></ol><div class="safe">Guided check only. No automatic database writes or service changes.</div><p><a href="https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/latency-optimization" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read beginner reference ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-api-html" data-keywords="unexpected token doctype html json login rewrite endpoint"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Unexpected HTML instead of JSON</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Check the request path and HTTP status in browser network tools.</li><li>Verify IIS forwards /admin/guardian/api/* to FastAPI rather than returning a static page.</li><li>Verify the backend route works directly from an authorized host.</li><li>Retest login, then record sanitized response headers if it fails.</li></ol><div class="safe">Guided check only. No automatic database writes or service changes.</div><p><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/iis/extensions/url-rewrite-module/using-the-url-rewrite-module" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read beginner reference ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-sql-connect" data-keywords="sql odbc 08s01 connection network server login refused"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>SQL Server connection failed</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Determine whether one or all tenants are affected.</li><li>Run the affected client self-check and check connectivity from the app server.</li><li>Have an administrator review SQL authentication and network route.</li><li>Retry only after connectivity is restored; never grant write permissions.</li></ol><div class="safe">Guided check only. No automatic database writes or service changes.</div><p><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/sql/connect/resolving-connectivity-errors" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read beginner reference ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-slow-sql" data-keywords="sql timeout slow queries expensive query execution latency"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>SQL queries are too slow</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Narrow to a report, date range, and affected client.</li><li>Check if it also fails with a one-day period.</li><li>Ask a DBA to review read-only execution plan and server load.</li><li>Do not add indexes or change LIS schema automatically.</li></ol><div class="safe">Guided check only. No automatic database writes or service changes.</div><p><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/relational-databases/performance/monitor-and-tune-for-performance" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read beginner reference ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-iis-502" data-keywords="iis 502 503 bad gateway service offline backend"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>HTTP 502/503 backend unavailable</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Verify Guardian/FastAPI health endpoint and Windows service status.</li><li>Check approved server event logs and reverse proxy routing.</li><li>If recent deployment broke startup, use an approved rollback.</li><li>Retest after authorized service recovery.</li></ol><div class="safe">Guided check only. No automatic database writes or service changes.</div><p><a href="https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/how-to-troubleshoot-common-http-error-codes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read beginner reference ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-pdf-export" data-keywords="pdf playwright chromium browser download broken"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>PDF generation or download fails</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm the equivalent text report works first.</li><li>Check server-side renderer errors and browser dependencies.</li><li>Verify patient selection uses UHID and authorized access.</li><li>Escalate with sanitized logs; never share identifiable patient reports.</li></ol><div class="safe">Guided check only. No automatic database writes or service changes.</div><p><a href="https://playwright.dev/python/docs/browsers" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read beginner reference ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-collection-mismatch" data-keywords="collection mismatch paidamount totalamount wrong revenue cash"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Collection totals differ from LIS</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Compare a single verified day against the LIS.</li><li>Check whether the client uses received payments or billed totals.</li><li>Review tenant-specific metric pins and source columns.</li><li>Suspend incorrect reports until reconciliation is verified.</li></ol><div class="safe">Guided check only. No automatic database writes or service changes.</div><p><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/t-sql/queries/select-transact-sql" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read beginner reference ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-schema-change" data-keywords="schema invalid column object missing table mapping"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Client schema changed</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Run client self-check and diagnostics.</li><li>Review the schema snapshot and detected columns.</li><li>Refresh cached mapping for that client only if appropriate.</li><li>Escalate mappings rather than altering client tables.</li></ol><div class="safe">Guided check only. No automatic database writes or service changes.</div><p><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/relational-databases/system-information-schema-views/columns-transact-sql" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read beginner reference ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-llm-request-times-out" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior AI timeout token streaming deadline"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>LLM request times out</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Compare a shorter question, inspect timeout/error logs, and verify provider response deadline.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-llm-answer-is-hallucinated" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior hallucination wrong fictional answer invented data"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>LLM answer is hallucinated</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Cross-check numerical claims with a read-only report; do not present unverified amounts.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-llm-answers-the-wrong-date" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior date today yesterday past backup ignored"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>LLM answers the wrong date</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Include an explicit date and compare returned period with the requested one.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-llm-ignores-a-branch-filter" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior branch location filter ignored answer"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>LLM ignores a branch filter</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Check whether branch name resolved to a unique location before querying.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-model-responds-in-the-wrong-language" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior translation locale language mismatch"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Model responds in the wrong language</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Inspect user language setting and prompt configuration without modifying tenant records.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-ai-api-key-rejected" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior 401 invalid key api credential"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>AI API key rejected</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Verify key presence and provider access through approved secrets management.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-ai-provider-billing-disabled" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior payment billing quota exhausted"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>AI provider billing disabled</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Check provider console billing limits through an authorized administrator.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-output-gets-cut-off" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior truncated max tokens incomplete answer"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Output gets cut off</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Check output token ceiling and streaming termination reasons.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-repeated-tool-call-loops" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior agent recursion repeated tools infinite"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Repeated tool-call loops</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Capture sanitized trace and ask engineering to inspect loop/iteration limits.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-direct-intent-returns-none" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior matched keyword none null handler"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Direct intent returns None</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Verify handler date parser and supported schema; no-data must not automatically trigger LLM.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-intent-phrase-collides-with-another-report" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior wrong handler substring precedence"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Intent phrase collides with another report</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Trace first matching keyword and prefer exact/specific routes.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-monthly-tat-reports-fail" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior unsupported period month 2026-08 date format"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Monthly TAT reports fail</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Check accepted period syntax in TAT dashboard and use one-day query as a temporary workaround.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-llm-streaming-stops-midway" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior stream interrupted websocket disconnected"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>LLM streaming stops midway</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Check proxy timeout and server log for interrupted streaming.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/handling-errors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-slow-responses-only-for-certain-clients" data-keywords="ai &amp; intent behavior client specific llm slow latency"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Slow responses only for certain clients</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Compare schema discovery timings and query timings for one affected tenant.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://fa