ck and timezone before comparing event timestamps.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/how-to-troubleshoot-common-http-error-codes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-activation-code-was-disabled" data-keywords="security, admin &amp; operations license disabled expired activation"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Activation code was disabled</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Check license status with an authorized administrator.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-admin-password-was-forgotten" data-keywords="security, admin &amp; operations admin password reset login"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Admin password was forgotten</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Follow approved identity verification and password reset process.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-unsafe-sql-was-attempted" data-keywords="security, admin &amp; operations sql injection unsafe delete update write"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Unsafe SQL was attempted</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Block execution and review read-only enforcement and audit logs.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-sensitive-data-appeared-in-logs" data-keywords="security, admin &amp; operations patient phi pii secrets logs"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Sensitive data appeared in logs</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Restrict log access and escalate sanitization defects.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-support-report-contains-private-data" data-keywords="security, admin &amp; operations support json sensitive leak"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Support report contains private data</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Do not distribute it; escalate sanitization issue.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-unexpected-access-to-client-records" data-keywords="security, admin &amp; operations unauthorized client access security"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Unexpected access to client records</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Revoke affected access via authorized process and alert security contact.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-user-role-cannot-see-a-report" data-keywords="security, admin &amp; operations access role doctor reception admin"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>User role cannot see a report</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Check role-to-report policy and account tier.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-schema-snapshot-changed-unexpectedly" data-keywords="security, admin &amp; operations schema drift change alert"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Schema snapshot changed unexpectedly</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Confirm change with client DBA and validate read-only report mappings.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-a-client-is-missing-from-monitoring" data-keywords="security, admin &amp; operations guardian client not listed status"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>A client is missing from monitoring</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Confirm activation, connectivity and recent signal reporting.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-alerts-are-too-noisy" data-keywords="security, admin &amp; operations alert duplicates notifications flood"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Alerts are too noisy</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Group by client/root cause and inspect thresholds.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-incident-recovery-was-not-confirmed" data-keywords="security, admin &amp; operations incident marked resolved prematurely"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Incident recovery was not confirmed</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Repeat the failed read-only report before closing an incident.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-how-to-prepare-a-support-handoff" data-keywords="security, admin &amp; operations support escalation handoff ticket"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>How to prepare a support handoff</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Capture client identifier, UTC/local time, user question, error and sanitized report.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" id="pb-extra-plan-safe-production-rollout" data-keywords="security, admin &amp; operations production release staging regression tenant"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Plan safe production rollout</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm which client, report and date range are affected.</li><li>Perform only authorized, read-only diagnostic checks first.</li><li>Test on backup clients, record baseline, deploy with rollback plan and validate tenants.</li><li>If unresolved, export a sanitized Guardian support report for engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client LIS tables or expose credentials during diagnosis.</div><p><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beginner documentation ↗</a></p></div></details><details class="playbook" data-keywords="tat sla reptimetime tattime compliance unavailable actual turn around month 2026" id="pb-tat-no-sla"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◷</span>TAT dashboard says compliance N/A</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Check whether the dashboard shows Actual TAT and completed-test counts. If yes, timestamps are working.</li><li>Use schema diagnostics to confirm investigation TATTIME/TATTYPE. Empty TATTIME means no verified SLA.</li><li>REPTIME/REPTIMETYPE may be a report-release SLA, so do not automatically assume it measures result-entry time.</li><li>Ask for a specific historical date if testing from a backup. If a month fails with “Unsupported period”, escalate a report period-parser defect.</li><li>Never present N/A as zero-percent compliance, or set fabricated default limits.</li></ol><div class="safe">Actual TAT can be computed without a defined SLA; official compliance cannot.</div></div></details><details class="playbook" data-keywords="intent routing llm fallback premiums keyword handler agent python wrong question" id="pb-intent-routing"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">⌘</span>Simple questions still use the LLM</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Try a known direct report: “Payment mode split” or “Top 10 tests”.</li><li>Check whether the updated agent/intents.py is deployed on the running server.</li><li>Ask the developer to verify the caller executes try_intent for this user's tier, before LLM fallback.</li><li>If the phrase matches but a handler returns None, check the mapped handler and supported date words.</li><li>Record the question and actual route; send the sanitized support report to engineering.</li></ol><div class="safe">Only restart the application service after a reviewed deployment. Do not edit client SQL tables to fix intent routing.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">▦</span> Excel collection export</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Verify whether the problem affects Today, Yesterday, or This Month.</li><li>Open Diagnostics and run a client self-check.</li><li>Review the collection metric and rejected mappings in schema diagnostics.</li><li>Compare the exported figures with verified SQL Server values. Billed totals must not be presented as cash collected.</li><li>If monthly only fails, send the support report to your technical contact.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not manually edit collection tables or overwrite another client's metric configuration.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">⌁</span> SQL Server connection failed</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Check whether other clients are responding normally.</li><li>Run the affected client's self-check once the circuit breaker allows a retry.</li><li>Ask the database administrator to verify server reachability and login permissions.</li><li>Check for a recent host, firewall, password, or network change.</li><li>Retry the same read-only report after connectivity is restored.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never change client database credentials or permissions without authorization.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span> AI Agent response failed</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Try a known instant report to separate SQL/database errors from AI-provider errors.</li><li>Check Guardian signals for rate limits, timeouts, or schema errors.</li><li>Confirm the LLM provider credentials and quota in the secure server settings.</li><li>If only one client is affected, run its self-check.</li><li>Escalate with the sanitized report if errors persist.</li></ol></div></details>
<details class="playbook"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">□</span> PDF / Smart Report failed</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Check whether a normal text report works for the same patient or UHID.</li><li>Confirm the patient identity and required authenticated results exist.</li><li>Check backend errors for template, renderer, or AI provider failures.</li><li>Confirm sufficient storage and browser-renderer availability on the app server.</li><li>Do not substitute another patient's data when a report cannot be generated.</li></ol></div></details>
<details class="playbook"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◈</span> Admin panel or sign-in issue</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Check whether the Guardian console page loads.</li><li>If login reports HTML instead of JSON, check the IIS rewrite rule for /admin/guardian/*.</li><li>Test the corresponding local FastAPI endpoint on the actual backend port.</li><li>Check admin-account status and authentication logs.</li><li>Avoid deleting or reseeding admin tables as a troubleshooting shortcut.</li></ol></div></details>
<details class="playbook"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">↗</span> Client schema changed</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Run Diagnostics → Compare schema snapshot.</li><li>View current schema diagnostics for missing columns and rejected pins.</li><li>Refresh only the client's schema cache and recheck.</li><li>Confirm any new column mapping with the LIS vendor or technical owner.</li><li>Escalate if the table family itself has changed.</li></ol><div class="safe">Schema refresh is not a database migration. It does not create or alter client tables.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="iis 404 staticfile rewrite proxy guardian route"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>IIS 404 — Guardian route</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Verify the FastAPI route responds from localhost on the server.</li><li>Open IIS URL Rewrite for the Sahasra site. Confirm /admin/guardian/* forwards to the FastAPI port.</li><li>Keep the specific Guardian rewrite above static-file rules and stop subsequent processing.</li><li>Retest the public HTTPS route.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not change client database settings to fix an IIS routing problem.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="unexpected token html json login authentication reverse proxy"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Unexpected token &lt; — HTML returned instead of JSON</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Check the failed browser request in Network → Response; an HTML page means the API route was not reached.</li><li>Verify /admin/guardian/api/* is forwarded to FastAPI by IIS.</li><li>Test the local FastAPI login endpoint and compare the public URL.</li><li>Ensure the rewrite preserves the request method and query string.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never paste admin passwords into logs or support tickets.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="guardian login 401 403 admin password credentials"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◈</span>Guardian sign-in rejected</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm you are using Guardian’s admin credentials, not a LIS activation code.</li><li>Review whether the admin account is enabled and whether credentials have expired.</li><li>Check backend authentication events and request status codes.</li><li>Have an authorized administrator reset credentials using the established admin procedure.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not modify or delete admin tables to reset a password.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="authorization bearer token forbidden expired"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>401 / 403 permission denied</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Sign out and sign back in to obtain a fresh session token.</li><li>Confirm the action uses an account with the correct administrative role.</li><li>If only one client fails, verify its assigned permissions and activation scope.</li><li>Escalate persistent 403s with a redacted support report.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not bypass access checks or share tokens.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="08S01 42000 timeout network sql odbc connection"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>SQL Server timeout or communication link failure</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Check whether the failure affects one client or all clients.</li><li>Run a client self-check if the database is reachable.</li><li>Ask the database administrator to check connection limits, VPN/firewall reachability, and server load.</li><li>For a long export, retry a smaller period only once, then escalate.</li></ol><div class="safe">Avoid repeated retries that overload SQL Server.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="invalid column name invalid object name schema mapping sql"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◈</span>Missing SQL table or column</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Inspect client schema diagnostics and rejected mappings.</li><li>Compare with the last known schema snapshot.</li><li>Refresh only that client’s schema profile if the database schema has changed.</li><li>Ask the LIS vendor to confirm the new column/table meaning before setting a pin.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never create or alter LIS tables to make a report run.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="paidamount totalamount billed amount mismatch reconciliation"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Incorrect collection totals</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Identify whether the report represents billed revenue or actual received payments.</li><li>Review the client’s collection metric pin and Amount Source fields.</li><li>Compare sample bills and totals independently with authorized SQL reporting.</li><li>Escalate if credits, refunds, concessions, or payment modes are being combined incorrectly.</li></ol><div class="safe">A TOTALAMOUNT fallback does not prove payment receipt.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="zeros paids total centromed fallback blank amount"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Collection Excel displays zeros</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Run a short daily export first and inspect both amount columns.</li><li>Check the client’s schema profile and effective collection metric.</li><li>Confirm the selected amount is based on the intended source and not a missing-column default.</li><li>Compare results with the LIS source records before approving the workbook.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not relabel billed amounts as cash collected.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="monthly excel 08S01 404 batch timeout memory"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◈</span>Monthly Excel fails but daily works</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Verify the Today and Yesterday exports succeed for the same client.</li><li>Check whether the month includes many branches or thousands of records.</li><li>Review backend export logs and database execution time.</li><li>Escalate for batching or streaming optimization if the whole month keeps failing.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not repeatedly run the full monthly report during a database outage.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="cash all delhi wrong branch mapping location mode"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Excel wrong branch or payment mode</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Inspect transaction rows for original LOCATIONID and MODE values.</li><li>Compare the rendered branch/payment labels against database master tables.</li><li>Confirm whether the report query supplies the actual mode or a default.</li><li>Escalate with sample anonymized rows showing the mismatch.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never assume every missing payment mode is Cash.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="recent patients register regdate uhid date sorting"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Recent patients missing or outdated</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Ask Recent Patients for the affected institution, then compare with the patient registration screen.</li><li>Check the patient-date field in schema diagnostics and the most recent REGDATE in SQL.</li><li>Verify the activation code points to the intended database, including test vs production.</li><li>Escalate if the underlying data is correct but results are stale.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not edit patient registration records to fix display issues.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="smart report pdf wrong uhid patient name authenticated"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◈</span>Smart Report shows wrong or missing patient</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Verify the report was requested using the correct UHID and institution.</li><li>Cross-check bill and investigation identifiers before relying on the output.</li><li>Confirm only authenticated investigation results are included where required.</li><li>Stop distribution and escalate any possible patient mixing immediately.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never use or distribute a report whose patient identity is uncertain.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="playwright chromium pdf failed template browser"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>PDF renderer unavailable</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Try a simple text report to isolate the problem to PDF generation.</li><li>Check backend logs for Chromium/Playwright or template exceptions.</li><li>Verify the approved renderer installation and server storage are intact.</li><li>Escalate if the process crashes or times out repeatedly.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not disable patient identity checks to make PDF export succeed.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="ai wrong answer hallucination intent misunderstood llm"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>AI gives a wrong intent or fabricated answer</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Repeat once with a clear question specifying client, date range and report.</li><li>Compare numeric answers with a verified LIS report or authorized SQL result.</li><li>Record the input and sanitized output for support.</li><li>If accuracy remains uncertain, stop relying on the AI result and escalate.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not treat fluent AI text as verified financial or clinical data.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="llm rate limit 429 quota provider ai unavailable" id="pb-llm-rate-limit"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◈</span>AI provider rate limit or outage</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Identify whether instant database reports still work.</li><li>Check the AI provider’s service status, available quota and configured model.</li><li>Wait for the provider rate limit to clear rather than repeatedly retrying.</li><li>Escalate if the provider credentials or subscription have changed.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not expose API keys in screenshots or support reports.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="breaker open paused five failures 60 seconds"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Circuit breaker paused a client</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Check the client name and failure category in Guardian status.</li><li>Allow the cooldown period to expire before retrying.</li><li>Run a self-check once; verify the underlying connection is stable.</li><li>Escalate repeated trips; other client databases should stay available.</li></ol><div class="safe">Never disable circuit breakers as the first troubleshooting step.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="license activation code institution expired disabled"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Activation code invalid or expired</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Confirm the entered code is assigned to the intended institution.</li><li>Check activation validity and expiry using authorized admin tools.</li><li>Check for network or clock issues affecting verification.</li><li>Contact the licensing administrator for renewal or correction.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not issue replacement activation codes from Guardian.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="json config clients utf8 bom pin metric profile"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◈</span>Config pin ignored or rejected</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Check that the file is under config/clients with the exact database name.</li><li>Open schema diagnostics to see whether the pin applied or was rejected.</li><li>Check JSON formatting and whether pinned column names exist in that database.</li><li>Refresh only this client’s cached profile and verify the effective metric.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not copy another client’s pin without verifying financial semantics.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="pharmacy stock inventory tables unavailable"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>One client has no pharmacy or inventory</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Check whether the institution has a pharmacy module at all.</li><li>Inspect capabilities and confirm expected pharmacy tables exist.</li><li>If tables are absent, explain that the report is unsupported.</li><li>Escalate for a supported pharmacy schema mapping rather than defaulting stock to zero.</li></ol><div class="safe">Unavailable stock data must not be reported as zero inventory.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="iis bad gateway service 502 503 backend restart"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Service unavailable / 502 / 503</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Check whether the FastAPI health endpoint is accessible locally.</li><li>Confirm the SahasraAIAgent Windows service is running.</li><li>Inspect recent application startup errors and the IIS reverse proxy target.</li><li>Escalate before restarting repeatedly if startup keeps failing.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not modify client SQL permissions to fix service routing.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="cache stale status 6 hours refresh browser"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◈</span>Dashboard or Guardian data looks stale</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Refresh the overview and note its timestamp/source where available.</li><li>Check whether a specific client’s schema profile needs refreshing.</li><li>Verify you are opening the expected environment and not a cached browser tab.</li><li>If backend values remain stale, gather a support report.</li></ol><div class="safe">Refresh is a read-side cache action, not a database repair.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="update rollback latest deploy previous build"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Deployment caused a regression</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Record the first failure time and the last known working release.</li><li>Run the standard smoke tests for at least three different LIS clients.</li><li>If critical functions broke, use the approved tested rollback procedure.</li><li>Escalate with release version, logs, and affected routes.</li></ol><div class="safe">Do not overwrite a working production release without a backup.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="tenant isolation leakage wrong database patient client"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◇</span>Data privacy or cross-client mix-up</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Stop the affected output and restrict access immediately.</li><li>Capture sanitized incident details: time, request type and client identifier.</li><li>Notify the organization’s security or technical escalation contact.</li><li>Do not retry with real patient data until tenant isolation is verified.</li></ol><div class="safe">Treat any cross-client patient exposure as a security incident.</div></div></details>
<details class="playbook" data-keywords="slow requests high concurrency memory cpu latency"><summary><span class="topic"><span class="topic-icon">◈</span>Slow performance under heavy load</span><span class="chevron">+</span></summary><div class="playbook-body"><ol><li>Check whether the issue is limited to a client or affects the whole service.</li><li>Identify the slow API action and reporting date range from logs.</li><li>Avoid parallel bulk exports while investigating database load.</li><li>Escalate for connection-pool, pagination, or query-plan review.</li></ol><div class="safe">Avoid broad SQL changes without testing on a nonproduction system.</div></div></details>
</div></section>
