<section class="section hidden" id="helpView"><div class="page-head"><div><div class="kicker">Guardian handbook</div><h1>Everything you need to run Guardian.</h1><p>A practical guide written for administrators—not developers.</p></div></div><div class="doc-label" id="help-docs">Beginner-friendly external guides</div><div class="doc-grid"><a class="doc-card" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/sql/connect/resolving-connectivity-errors"><b>🗄️ SQL Server connections ↗</b><span>Microsoft Learn · diagnose login, network, and timeouts</span></a><a class="doc-card" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/iis/extensions/url-rewrite-module/using-the-url-rewrite-module"><b>🌐 IIS URL Rewrite ↗</b><span>Microsoft Learn · understand why API routes show HTML or 404</span></a><a class="doc-card" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/how-to-troubleshoot-common-http-error-codes"><b>🧭 HTTP errors explained ↗</b><span>DigitalOcean · friendly guide to 401, 404, 500 and 502 errors</span></a><a class="doc-card" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/deployment/"><b>⚙️ FastAPI deployment ↗</b><span>FastAPI · app startup and deployment concepts</span></a><a class="doc-card" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/relational-databases/security/authentication-access/permissions-database-engine"><b>🔒 SQL permissions ↗</b><span>Microsoft Learn · understand read-only database access</span></a><a class="doc-card" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/sc-query"><b>🖥️ Windows services ↗</b><span>Microsoft Learn · how to inspect service state</span></a></div><p class="fix-alert">External guides explain general troubleshooting. Follow your organization's approval process before changing IIS, service settings, permissions, or credentials.</p><div class="help-index"><a href="#help-purpose">What Guardian does</a><a href="#help-start">Getting started</a><a href="#help-buttons">What each button means</a><a href="#help-failures">Troubleshooting</a><a href="#help-limits">What Guardian cannot do</a></div>
<div class="panel"><div class="panel-content" style="padding:30px 36px"><div class="help-block" id="help-purpose"><h2>1. What is Sahasra Guardian?</h2><p>Guardian is a support workspace for the Sahasra AI Agent. It reports recent client-specific errors, offers plain-language troubleshooting, and checks whether a client database is reachable and its expected schema can be read. It does <b>not</b> replace the main Admin panel; the two serve different purposes.</p></div><hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin:27px 0"><div class="help-block" id="help-start"><h2>2. First-time use</h2><ol><li>Open the Guardian Console link on your deployed Sahasra website.</li><li>Sign in using the same authorized admin account.</li><li>The Overview page opens automatically; the sign-in form disappears.</li><li>Review incidents. A temporarily paused client usually means repeated database failures triggered its circuit breaker.</li><li>To investigate a client, choose <b>Diagnostics</b> at the top and enter its activation code.</li><li>Start with <b>Run self-check</b>, then use the other tools only as needed.</li><li>Use <b>Playbooks</b> for recovery steps, or export the support report if escalation is necessary.</li></ol></div><hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin:27px 0"><div class="help-block" id="help-buttons"><h2>3. What each button does</h2><div style="overflow:auto"><table class="help-table"><thead><tr><th>Button</th><th>What happens</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Refresh status</td><td>Requests the current Guardian status and recent incidents from the backend.</td></tr><tr><td>Run self-check</td><td>Checks one client's connection, available schema information, and configured mappings. It is intended to be read-only.</td></tr><tr><td>View schema diagnostics</td><td>Displays what Guardian detected about the client's report capabilities and configuration.</td></tr><tr><td>Compare schema snapshot</td><td>Compares the current client schema with the previously saved snapshot. Its snapshot metadata may be updated, but LIS tables are not supposed to be modified.</td></tr><tr><td>Refresh cached profile</td><td>Rebuilds the selected client's cached schema profile without editing its LIS data.</td></tr><tr><td>Download support report</td><td>Downloads a sanitized JSON diagnostic report to share with technical support.</td></tr><tr><td>Sign out</td><td>Clears the Guardian session token held in this browser page.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin:27px 0"><div class="help-block" id="help-failures"><h2>4. What to do when something fails</h2><ol><li>Note the <b>client</b>, <b>time</b>, and <b>action</b> that failed.</li><li>Open <b>Diagnostics</b> and perform a client self-check.</li><li>Open <b>Playbooks</b> and follow the matching guide.</li><li>If the error remains, click <b>Download support report</b>.</li><li>Share it securely with your designated technical contact. Never send passwords or full patient data.</li></ol><p>If the Guardian login itself fails, check whether IIS is rewriting <code>/admin/guardian/*</code> requests to FastAPI rather than serving a static 404 or HTML error page.</p></div><hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin:27px 0"><div class="help-block" id="help-limits"><h2>5. Limits and safety</h2><ul><li>Guardian can explain errors and run the supported checks. It cannot guarantee repair of a new code bug.</li><li>Do not treat automatic collection-column detection as proof of accounting meaning; distinguish billed amounts from received money.</li><li>Do not grant write access to client LIS databases just to make a report work.</li><li>Keep backups, known-good app releases, and a named technical escalation contact.</li><li>Not all incidents are detected immediately; status reflects what the deployed backend has recorded.</li></ul></div></div></div></section>
<div class="footer">Sahasra Guardian · AthenTech · Safe operations, clear answers</div>
